{"assets":["/statement-assets/20f0379018ae4f941edb19eaa978cb81f5359e01ff8c697f93271b3036158001.png","/statement-assets/ddf99211e2d2a4b32c56a053a7884df3a7c2305ceb7db1ab086e54629d86abea.png","/statement-assets/13674bdd580acf63d9257686f409a7736580b2b4c2285052bde98f924a7efe5d.png","/statement-assets/5be48f5a9a213c35cb93cd5a5b47c78be6fe1b1a92383c712118b1f1b186441f.png","/statement-assets/208d737f0f5a67b9b27d8623cd8af10f687a9dd63c982ad02dfd2e514e4fff0d.png","/statement-assets/45a4f54b4bfcc59faab31ebd37fd87ea8fdfd9e77104dc93f8197c79c8539402.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"643","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Bearish Fanpages"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is a social website with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" fanpages, numbered "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" through "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". There are also "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" companies, and the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th company owns the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th fanpage."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recently, the website created a feature called following. Each fanpage must choose exactly one other fanpage to follow."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The website doesn’t allow a situation where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" follows "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":" and at the same time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":" follows "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":". Also, a fanpage can't follow itself."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s say that fanpage "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" follows some other fanpage "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j0"},{"kind":"text","text":". Also, let’s say that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" is followed by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" other fanpages "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j1, j2, ..., jk"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then, when people visit fanpage "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" they see ads from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k + 2"},{"kind":"text","text":" distinct companies: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i, j0, j1, ..., jk"},{"kind":"text","text":". Exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" people subscribe (like) the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th fanpage, and each of them will click exactly one add. For each of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" companies "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j0, j1, ..., jk"},{"kind":"text","text":", exactly "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/20f0379018ae4f941edb19eaa978cb81f5359e01ff8c697f93271b3036158001.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" people will click their ad. Remaining "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/ddf99211e2d2a4b32c56a053a7884df3a7c2305ceb7db1ab086e54629d86abea.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" people will click an ad from company "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the owner of the fanpage)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The total income of the company is equal to the number of people who click ads from this copmany."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Limak and Radewoosh ask you for help. Initially, fanpage "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" follows fanpage "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"fi"},{"kind":"text","text":". Your task is to handle "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" queries of three types:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 i j"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" — fanpage "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" follows fanpage "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":" from now. It's guaranteed that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" didn't follow "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":" just before the query. Note an extra constraint for the number of queries of this type (below, in the Input section). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 i"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" — print the total income of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th company. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" — print two integers: the smallest income of one company and the biggest income of one company. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 ≤ n ≤ 100 000"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ q ≤ 100 000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of fanpages and the number of queries, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t1, t2, ..., tn"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ti ≤ 1012"},{"kind":"text","text":") where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" denotes the number of people subscribing the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th fanpage."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f1, f2, ..., fn"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ fi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Initially, fanpage "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" follows fanpage "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"fi"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines follow. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them describes the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th query. The first number in the line is an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"typei"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ typei ≤ 3"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the type of the query."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There will be at most "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"50 000"},{"kind":"text","text":" queries of the first type. There will be at least one query of the second or the third type (so, the output won't be empty)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's guaranteed that at each moment a fanpage doesn't follow itself, and that no two fanpages follow each other."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each query of the second type print one integer in a separate line - the total income of the given company. For each query of the third type print two integers in a separate line - the minimum and the maximum total income, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 12\n10 20 30 40 50\n2 3 4 5 2\n2 1\n2 2\n2 3\n2 4\n2 5\n1 4 2\n2 1\n2 2\n2 3\n2 4\n2 5\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10\n36\n28\n40\n36\n9\n57\n27\n28\n29\n9 57\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/13674bdd580acf63d9257686f409a7736580b2b4c2285052bde98f924a7efe5d.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the sample test, there are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" fanpages. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i·10"},{"kind":"text","text":" subscribers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On drawings, numbers of subscribers are written in circles. An arrow from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"B"},{"kind":"text","text":" means that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":" follows "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"B"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The left drawing shows the initial situation. The first company gets income "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/5be48f5a9a213c35cb93cd5a5b47c78be6fe1b1a92383c712118b1f1b186441f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" from its own fanpage, and gets income "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/208d737f0f5a67b9b27d8623cd8af10f687a9dd63c982ad02dfd2e514e4fff0d.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"-nd fanpage. So, the total income is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5 + 5 = 10"},{"kind":"text","text":". After the first query (\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\") you should print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The right drawing shows the situation after a query \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 4 2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (after which fanpage "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" follows fanpage "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Then, the first company still gets income "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" from its own fanpage, but now it gets only "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/45a4f54b4bfcc59faab31ebd37fd87ea8fdfd9e77104dc93f8197c79c8539402.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"-nd fanpage. So, the total income is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5 + 4 = 9"},{"kind":"text","text":" now."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"643D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/643/problem/D"}